 `tests/test_desktop_service.py` uses a real temporary SQLite `OperationStore` with explicit fixture adapters and verifies all eight coordinator routes, durable claim-before-callback ordering, same-key replay and body conflict, cross-coordinator ownership noninterference, optional-field type validation, pending/unknown non-replay, same-session serialization across windows, process-birth/lease invalidation, endpoint/model cross-binding, fingerprint invalidation, typed `NodePath` validation, dual shell permission, capture scope rejection, and save-copy hash/source-preservation handling. `tests/test_desktop_capture.py` exercises a non-GUI spawned child, bounded timeout/child-only termination, output-path confinement, size/header/hash validation and refusal off Windows. The latest four-file software regression run covers `test_desktop_service.py`, `test_desktop_capture.py`, `test_desktop_win32_identity.py`, and `test_desktop_control_wiring.py`: 51 passed on Python 3.12.13 / pytest 9.1.1. Its source hashes and output are recorded in [the Desktop software regression receipt](../evidence/w25_block_other_clients/desktop_software_retest_20260926T2230Z/desktop_software_regression.json). These tests do not establish native control support or any T004/T051/T052/T054 acceptance result.
+
+
+## Historical isolated W25 contract003 Phase1 software scope (2026-10-02)
+
+This successor exists only in the isolated source copy. It adds a lazy product PyObjC AX/Quartz prerequisite observer with exact target-window mapping, non-prompt caller permission reads and bounded AX metadata. Codex CUA/observer permissions are not product acceptance. The factory defaults to the existing metadata-only adapter; opting into the observer does not enable controls. Missing/ambiguous mapping, dependencies or permission refuse; no focused-window fallback, screenshot, guessed COMSOL selector, input or launch is performed by the observer. All seven control methods, current-model observation, Shell/save/cancel remain unsupported without actual build-specific evidence.
+
+The Desktop queue now supports explicit JSON-encoded typed ModelRef resolution/inspection through the existing ExecutionService.inspect_evidence and model_project_binding, exact active durable claim and existing ProjectAuthority. It performs a fresh scoped parameters+shallow-tree identity read, not full-model identity/dirty preservation or a GUI binding. Wrong project/epoch, dirty or active model, or an external change refuses. Opaque identifiers without a trusted mapping still refuse. Registered source resolution reuses existing immutable project-artifact integrity/host scope; save-copy destination authorization reuses existing non-overwrite/symlink-confined ArtifactStore path policy. No recursive daemon dispatch, second durable claim, backend accessor or coordinator post-fingerprint semantics change.
+
+This Phase1 snapshot preceded the Phase2b single-claim managed copy-load callback. The later software callback loads a project-authorized copy into a registered managed session; it does not perform or certify native Desktop save-copy, current-window binding, or Desktop Shell actions. Generic backend.invoke/managed-server Java still cannot substitute for an observed Desktop Shell provider. Original eight actions and T004/T023/T051/T052/T054 are still NOT_RUN/unaccepted. Software fixture evidence and retained first-run failures remain historical. Current scoped integration software receipts are recorded under `docs/full_project_continuation_v2/evidence/w25_integration/`; they do not imply native acceptance. No live repository promotion, Windows/Intel compatibility or matrix certification is implied.
